{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Common.FormalResidue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Common.FormalResidue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.exists_antideriv_iff_fresidue_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.exists_antideriv_iff_fresidue_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L93-L114","doc":"**The residue is the complete obstruction to exactness** (char-0 field):\na formal Laurent expansion is a termwise derivative iff its residue\nvanishes. Forward direction is `fresidue_fderiv`; the converse divides each\ncoefficient by its shifted exponent, which is where `CharZero` enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.antideriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.antideriv","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L87-L91","doc":"Candidate termwise antiderivative: `(t⁻¹ ↦ dropped, tᵉ⁻¹ ↦ tᵉ/e)`.\nOnly its values at `e ≠ 0` matter; the value at `0` is a free integration\nconstant, set to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_jet_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_jet_succ","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L75-L79","doc":"Every positive-order classical jet is exact, so its residue vanishes at\nevery point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.jet_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.jet_succ","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.jet_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.jet_zero","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.jet","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L65-L69","doc":"The `n`-th classical jet of a local expansion: `n`-fold termwise\nderivative (the coefficient-level face of `X^{(n)} = dⁿX/dzⁿ` on the curve). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_fderiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_fderiv","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**The residue of an exact form vanishes**: the `t⁻¹` coefficient of a\ntermwise derivative is `((−1)+1)·f(0) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fderiv_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fderiv_smul","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L54-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fderiv_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fderiv_add","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L50-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_smul","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L47-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_add","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L44-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue_zero","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fderiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fderiv","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L38-L40","doc":"Termwise derivative of a formal Laurent expansion:\n`(Σ c_e tᵉ)' = Σ (e+1)·c_{e+1} tᵉ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FormalResidue.fresidue","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/FormalResidue.lean#L34-L36","doc":"Formal residue of a local Laurent expansion, presented as its coefficient\nfunction `f : ℤ → R`: the coefficient of `t⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}